  "description": "Field frame vectors (protocol/field-frames.md, RFC 0001 Amendment 7). hkdf_sha256: RFC 5869 appendix A.1-A.3 as printed in the RFC. field_key: HKDF-SHA256 of join.json's join_key with no salt and the info 'atalaia field frame v1', 16 bytes. valid: each body decodes to its fields and re-encodes byte for byte; sealed with field_key and the given nonce it is the frame, which opens back to the body (AES-128-CCM, 8-byte MIC, AAD the header without hop_limit). hop_limit_ignored opens to valid[1]'s body. invalid_frames do not open (reason: header, length or mac). invalid_bodies are refused by the body decoder. optional_key_skipped decodes like an announce without key 20. split: a join payload's invite chunks (153 bytes, the last shorter). nonces: nonce_key is HKDF-SHA256 of the join key with the info 'atalaia field nonce v1', 32 bytes; a nonce is HMAC-SHA256(nonce_key, sender)[0..7] | boot (3 bytes) | ctr (2 bytes), big-endian; source: a sender's run after a stored boot count of 41 (its first two nonces, then the last of boot 42 and the first of boot 43), which leaves 43 stored. Generated by tools/field_frame_vectors.py.",
